/*
  core/masks/habituated_approve.spthy -- f_H for the NEW Habituated mask, APPROVE_REQ action.
  (Plan §3: the strongest single research-backed addition; MFA prompt-bombing, warning fatigue.)

  Habituated is NOT Careless: a Careless user disengages (timeout); a Habituated user
  ACTIVELY approves -- reflexively, without reading -- to make the prompt go away. It is
  Habituated is the CURRENT mask (gated by core/transitions/mask_state.spthy via RespMask, set
  by the Shift rule once sigma8 is active): it approves a prompt of ANY kind, including an
  adversary-'injected' one -- exactly what prompt-bombing weaponizes. auto_approve() (plan §2).
*/

rule Approve_Habituated:
    [ !Prompt(P, pid, kind) ]
  --[ Approve(P, pid, 'Habituated'), RespMask(P,'Habituated'), AutoApprove(P, pid),
      Mask(P,'Attentive','Habituated'), Answered(pid) ]->
    [ !Approved(P, pid, 'Habituated') ]
